    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Liddane House enjoys an enviable setting in the popular coastal town of Kilkee, one of West Clare’s most sought-after seaside destinations. \r\n\r\nRenowned for its spectacular coastline, beautiful horseshoe-shaped Kilkee Beach and dramatic cliff scenery, Kilkee offers an exceptional quality of life with a wonderful selection of cafés, restaurants, pubs, shops and local amenities.\r\n\r\n The property is ideally positioned just 300 metres from Kilkee Beach, placing the stunning Atlantic coastline quite literally on the doorstep. The famous Kilkee Cliffs, scenic cliff walks and the renowned Pollock Holes are all within easy reach. The town also provides excellent opportunities for swimming, surfing, diving, walking and golfing, with Kilkee Golf Club located nearby. \r\n\r\nKilkee forms part of the spectacular Wild Atlantic Way and is ideally placed for exploring the wider West Clare coastline, with Kilrush, Doonbeg, Loop Head and the wider attractions of County Clare all within easy reach. \r\n\r\nLiddane House is a charming three-bedroom terraced cottage, believed to date from the mid-1800s, offering a rare opportunity to acquire a property rich in character and history in the heart of Kilkee.\r\n\r\nIdeally positioned on the eastern side of Grattan Street, the property enjoys a convenient location within easy reach of Kilkee’s many amenities. \r\n\r\nThe accommodation is thoughtfully laid out, extending to an entrance hall, reception room and separate sitting room, leading through to a dining room, kitchen and utility area. The first floor provides three bedrooms, offering comfortable accommodation for family living or a coastal retreat. \r\n\r\nTo the rear, the property benefits from a generous private yard and garden, which is not overlooked and provides a wonderful outdoor space with excellent potential for entertaining, relaxing or simply enjoying the peaceful surroundings. \r\n\r\nWith its mid-19th-century origins, traditional cottage character, generous rear garden and enviable coastal location, Liddane House presents an exciting opportunity to own a truly distinctive home in one of County Clare’s most popular seaside towns.\r\n\r\nServices:\r\n\r\nMains water, mains sewer, electric storage heating\r\n\r\nAsking price:\r\n\r\nOffers in Excess of €395,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation:\r\n\r\nThe following is the accommodation and approximate room dimensions\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall (Ceramic Tiled flooring & store)                                               4.34 x 3.27\r\n\r\nSitting Room                                                                                                         4.71 x 3.99\r\n\r\nDining Room (Ceramic tiled flooring)                                                               5.00 x 3.82\r\n\r\nKitchen (Ceramic tiled flooring, fitted kitchen, cooker & extractor)           3.82 x 3.24\r\n\r\nUtility/Hotpress                                                                                                   3.82 x 1.98\r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom (Ensuite- fully tiled)                                                             4.79 x 2.99\r\n\r\nBedroom 2                                                                                                           4.04 x 3.00\r\n\r\nBedroom 3                                                                                                           4.76 x 2.95\r\n\r\nBathroom (Fully tiled)                                                                                         2.13 x 1.73\r\n\r\nThe total floor area is approximately 155.73 sq.mtrs (1,676sq.ft)\r\n\r\nExterior:\r\n\r\nLiscannor stone patio\r\nWalled in garden\r\nDerelict outbuilding\r\nSide entrance"
      },
